  "question": {
    "text": "If a function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> satisfy the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8704;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></math> and the function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is continuous at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, then"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is continuous for all positive real values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is continuous for all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> for all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "None of the above",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8757;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;be any point</p><p>Now, at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></munder><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>a</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>h</mi></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>a</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>a</mi></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is continuous at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> is any arbitrary point.</p><p>Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is continuous for all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>.</p>"
  }
